ready-delivered ids probably can be re-requested. Recent results show recall with requested ids including already delivered ones (ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3 page:10 was requested and queued). So re-delivery is possible.\n\nBut the pending batch (8 pages) is being delivered now. I should write notes from originals already received. This action: write the reasoning note? I lack the p.10 quote.\n\nAlternative approach: write reasoning note now with only what I have verified (ToT verbatim + self-consistency mentioned with page 10, no quote), then update it later after recalling page 10. Notes can be updated multiple times; last one is final.\n\nActually simpler: use this action to recall page 10 AND write the ToT-based partial note? Both in one action — recall queues, write_note uses ev id from p.13. Fine. Then next action has page 10 text, and I update the reasoning note.\n\nLet me do: write_note for reasoning (partial: ToT answered + self-consistency noted with page 10) with evidence ['ev-4049593a30e2846f8394'], plus recall(['ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3']).\n\nNote content must be in prose and passed verbatim as literal. Keep 20-1500 chars.\n\nLet me compose note (avoiding claiming verbatim quote for self-consistency yet). Content:\n\n\"reasoning 主题笔记（初版，p.10–13）：\n1) Self Consistency 的选择规则：对同一问题采样多条推理路径，再按多数投票（majority voting）从各路径的最终答案中选出出现次数最多的答案，而不是取某条路径的中间步骤（p.10–11，§2.1）。\n2) Tree of Thoughts 的两种搜索控制器（p.13 原文）：'The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.' 即 breadth-first 与 depth-first；ToT 用 generation prompt、evaluation prompt 与外部搜索算法三者配合（p.13）。\n局限：外部搜索需外部记忆记住已走过的分支（p.15）。\"\n\nThat's Chinese notes — fine. Length ok.\n\nInclude English quote from p.13 verbatim: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" Check the delivered text: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a\\ndepth-first controller.\" Yes.\n\nEvidence ids: ev-4049593a30e2846f8394 (p.13).\n\nBut wait—writing a note before knowing self-consistency verbatim could be revised later. OK.\n\nAlso I should keep moving on pending delivery. Just do both in one block."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8936, "completion_tokens": 1532, "total_tokens": 10468, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1233}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 4584}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
