 Self Consistency majority voting; ToT breadth-first and depth-first. Where is Self Consistency described? Page 10-11 presumably. I haven't got the exact quote text visible now (ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3 page:10, ev-0aaa960f62d9cf1689f1 page:11 were delivered earlier). I don't have their text in this conversation window now. I could re-recall them later.\n\nFor now, continue reading. Recall next batch.\n\nI'll recall pages 19-22."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8344, "completion_tokens": 529, "total_tokens": 8873, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 447}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 3992}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
