 controller.\" — that may be a paraphrase, risky.\n\nActually, I should reconsider: the notes I have were written in earlier turns, and the exact quotes I'll need for evidence in report.json. The evaluator checks quotes appear in the PDF page text. So I need verifiable quotes.\n\nOptions: recall specific pages again? The instruction says don't reread unchanged sources, but recall of page evidence for quote verification may be legitimate; however each recall consumes requests (25 left).\n\nStrategy: continue receiving batch pages 21-28 next, write tool_use/multi_agent notes as data arrives, then outlook. Then build report from notes.\n\nSince the pending batch follows successful actions automatically, I should do something minimal — e.g., a write_note that is genuine for existing content, or just recall? Actually \"The next batch follows successful actions automatically.\" So just do a benign action like updating the plan or printing task_status? They said don't call read_pdf/task_status just to advance. Hmm, but the pending batch will be delivered with my next action. Maybe write the reasoning note refinement? But that requires exact quotes I don't currently have visible.\n\nActually maybe I can recall pages 21-28 explicitly, since the queue has them. But that's what's pending. Let me just do a small action: update_plan marking nothing changed? Better: use read_file? No.\n\nPerhaps recall a couple of the pending ids (e.g., pages 21-22) to advance and get more content — recall returns queued only, delivery in next feedback. The delivery mechanism: my action triggers delivery of the pending batch along with feedback. So a minimal action suffices. I'll do update_plan to keep statuses (same titles, reading still doing), which is a successful action.\n\nActually better to do something useful: I could write a note on reasoning improvements if I have quotes... I don't. Let me do update_plan.\n\nHmm, but maybe I can recall pages 21-28 to reduce ambiguity about which batch next. The selector chooses next batch anyway. I'll recall ['ev-e5b9499e130a976eefe2'...'ev-eb42e63472799e638c3f'] to indicate priority, plus overview plan. Let's just do update_plan + recall for pages 21-24 ids.\n\nCareful: output ONE fenced Python block."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8819, "completion_tokens": 933, "total_tokens": 9752, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 738}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 4467}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
